desc:ReaProof Gain BROKEN (stalls at extreme)
// Deliberately-broken variant for the JSFX battery's parameter sweep: at high
// gain settings (>= +18 dB) @sample enters a nested runaway loop and the
// audio thread stalls — the classic real-world JSFX failure mode (unbounded
// while()/file_avail() read loops; catalog items 4/9 territory). A JSFX
// cannot emit NaN/Inf into the graph (the host scrubs non-finite output and
// clamps to ±1 — live-verified on 7.75), so a STALL is the honest way a
// sweep-reachable extreme breaks a render: the offline render never
// completes and the battery fails it via its crash/hang timeout (§1.7).
// The loops are nested so any per-loop iteration cap cannot save the render.

slider1:0<-24,24,0.01>Gain (dB)

in_pin:left input
in_pin:right input
out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output

@slider
gain = 10^(slider1/20);
stall = (slider1 >= 18) ? 1 : 0;

@sample
stall ? (
  i = 0;
  while (i < 100000000) (
    j = 0;
    while (j < 100000000) ( j += 1; );
    i += 1;
  );
);
spl0 *= gain;
spl1 *= gain;
